 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Секретное лекарство  (The Secret Medicine)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Barinov is still angry with the judge who took away his licence, and he and the cook Senya have a plan for her birthday dinner. Senya has brought a strong \"remedy\", and the chef wants to know exactly what it does. Here's the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сеня, ты принёс то особое средство?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, шеф, это сильное средство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это вообще новое мощное лекарство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Как быстро оно начинает действовать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Очень быстро, шеф, буквально сразу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Одна таблетка решает все ваши проблемы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "И какой будет точный эффект?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обещаю, клиент от унитаза не отойдёт!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Отлично, судья запомнит этот юбилей!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы добавим таблетку в её суп?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нет, положим порошок прямо на гуся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы другие гости не отравились.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не бойся, я сделаю всё лично.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's follow the plan.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сеня, ты принёс то особое средство?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, did you bring that special remedy?' The word for brought, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "принёс",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is a man's action word for carrying here. The word for any means or remedy is the basis for \"that special means\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "то особое средство?",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, шеф, это сильное средство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, chef, this is a strong remedy.' The word for strong, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "сильное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is built from the word for strength. It has an \"it\" shape because it matches ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "средство.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это вообще новое мощное лекарство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is brand new powerful medicine.' Translates to \"totally new\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "вообще новое",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". The word for powerful, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "мощное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is built from the word for power, and a drug from the pharmacy is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "лекарство.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Как быстро оно начинает действовать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How quickly does it start to act?' The word for it, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "оно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", has an \"it\" shape to match the medicine. Translates to \"begins to act\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "начинает действовать?",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Очень быстро, шеф, буквально сразу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Very quickly, chef, literally right away.' The word for literally, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "буквально",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", has the word for letter inside it, just as the English word literally does. Translates to \"at once\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "сразу.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Одна таблетка решает все ваши проблемы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'One pill solves all your problems.' The word for one, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Одна",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", has a \"girl\" shape because ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "таблетка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " does. The word for solves is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "решает",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", and translates to \"all your problems\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "все ваши проблемы.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "И какой будет точный эффект?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what will be the exact effect?' With a \"boy\" shape to match the effect, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "какой",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " asks \"what kind of\". Translates to \"will be\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "будет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which is all that is needed for things happening later. The word for exact is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "точный",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обещаю, клиент от унитаза не отойдёт!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I promise, the customer will not leave the toilet!' The word for \"I promise\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обещаю,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " and after the linking word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "от",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the toilet becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "унитаза",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". Translates to \"won't step away from\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "не отойдёт!",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Отлично, судья запомнит этот юбилей!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Excellent, the judge will remember this anniversary!' The word for will remember, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "запомнит",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", uses a starting piece for fixing something in memory. The word for a round-number birthday or anniversary is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "юбилей!",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы добавим таблетку в её суп?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Shall we add the pill into her soup?' The word for \"we'll add\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "добавим",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". The word for her, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "её",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", never changes its ending, and translates to \"into the soup\" (if we remove \"her\"), using the linking word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " before ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "суп?",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нет, положим порошок прямо на гуся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, we will put the powder directly on the goose.' Translates to \"we'll lay\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "положим",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", for putting something down flat. The word for powder is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "порошок",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", and onto the goose is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "на гуся.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы другие гости не отравились.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The main thing is that other guests do not get poisoned.' Translates to \"the main thing, so that\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". The word for \"got poisoned\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "отравились.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", has an ending for more than one person, and it follows the \"so that\" word in a shape for things that already happened.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не бойся, я сделаю всё лично.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not fear, I will do everything personally.' Translates to the friendly command \"don't be afraid\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не бойся,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " and translates to \"I'll do everything\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "сделаю всё",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". The word for personally is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "лично.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сеня, ты принёс то особое средство?",
   "gap": 0.5
